{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TensorProduct"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"First"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Second"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices and their indices are as in ","type":"text"},{"code":"CartesianProduct","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The row of (g, h) lists ","type":"text"},{"code":"(g′, h′)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each entry g′ of G’s row of g and each entry h′ of H’s row of h, G outer. Rows are computed from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the factors’ index rows and never hash.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge’s position is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position(first: e, second: f, reversed:)"},{"type":"text","text":": G’s edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"type":"text","text":" and H’s edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":". In an undirected product two non-loop edges {a, b} and {c, d} give two edges, the straight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"{(a, c), (b, d)} and the reversed {(a, d), (b, c)}, where a, c are the edges’ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"u"},{"type":"text","text":" ends; when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"either is a self-loop they coincide and there is one, not reversed. A row lists a factor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop from its first appearance only, so every product edge has each of its ends once in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rows. Directed, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed"},{"type":"text","text":" is always false, and the product has edge indices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"index(e)·m_H + index(f)"},{"type":"text","text":" when both factors have them; undirected it has none, because a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop changes how many edges a factor pair gives."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:13GraphProducts13TensorProductV","modules":[{"name":"GraphProducts"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TensorProduct"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"TensorProduct.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct.swift#L42"},"title":"TensorProduct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TensorProduct","kind":"identifier"}]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/Position","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/UndirectedEdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/UndirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/TensorProduct\/UndirectedIndexRow"],"title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Inst